   "persona": "Buddy Johnston is a 40‑year‑old accountant with a passion for art who balances meticulous number‑crunching with spontaneous weekend drives, a habit of over‑collecting vintage camera gear, and a tendency to procrastinate on filing tax drafts until the last minute.",
   "professional_persona": "Buddy Johnston leverages fifteen years of corporate and small‑business accounting expertise—mastering QuickBooks, Excel, and SAP—to deliver clear audit reports and tax filings, while their curiosity for art fuels unconventional problem‑solving and client communication, even as their spontaneous nature occasionally battles strict deadline structures on their path to senior auditor and a boutique practice serving creative entrepreneurs.",
   "cultural_background": "Buddy was born and raised in the suburbs of Dallas, Texas, in a working‑class white family with Protestant roots. The local culture emphasized hospitality, community gatherings, and a strong work ethic, while also exposing him to the region’s vibrant arts scene and diverse culinary traditions. Growing up in Irving, he absorbed a blend of traditional Southern values—family loyalty, modesty, and respect for authority—and the cosmopolitan openness of a growing metropolitan area. This background shapes his polite, cooperative demeanor and his appreciation for both classic Texan customs such as barbecues and high‑school football, and new ideas, especially within the visual arts and music communities."
  },
